574
00:55:33,984 --> 00:55:39,812
Now time has come to focus on IP-based startups, IP-based unicorns going forward.

575
00:55:40,064 --> 00:55:54,544
I think that will require more product definitions, government becoming an enabler because in these deep tech space, despite whatever the VCs and others may say, I think that patient capital is still a big challenge in India.

576
00:55:54,944 --> 00:55:59,264
And that's the reason many of these companies still go abroad seeking funding, right?

577
00:55:59,344 --> 00:56:01,504
I have seen a lot of good startups do that.

578
00:56:01,710 --> 00:56:04,304
But I think patient capital is still a big challenge.

579
00:56:04,590 --> 00:56:11,184
Government, you know, for the first time now in the last five years, is able to say that we are willing to fund startups, right?

580
00:56:11,438 --> 00:56:14,212
Bigger amounts, 20 crores, 30 crores, kind of a money.

581
00:56:14,384 --> 00:56:15,664
I think all credit to them.

582
00:56:15,744 --> 00:56:17,904
We need to do it at scale, right?

583
00:56:17,984 --> 00:56:25,824
Not those 10 companies, 20 companies, but you know, there's a lot of talent, and that also requires you know, some institutional mechanism.

584
00:56:26,224 --> 00:56:28,384
Right now, what happens is as an academic, right?

585
00:56:28,558 --> 00:56:32,544
Many academics can develop technologies up to a proof of concept, right?

586
00:56:32,750 --> 00:56:36,144
At a level where you know I can show in a laboratory that it works.

587
00:56:36,430 --> 00:56:41,584
It's a I paid, filed a patent, I have a US patent, I have done all of that, you know, it works, right?

588
00:56:41,744 --> 00:56:48,064
But then to make it a product, that is where we call TRL 3, technology readiness level 3, maybe, right?

589
00:56:48,304 --> 00:56:49,284
A proof of concept.

590
00:56:49,518 --> 00:56:56,784
But to start selling something in the market, you are requiring TRL 7, TRL 8, all of that kind of a level, right?

591
00:56:56,944 --> 00:57:07,172
You have to now build more of those technologies, test it in the field, go through the whole field trials, understand the challenges, keep tweaking it, keep it reliable, get the certifications.

592
00:57:07,406 --> 00:57:10,224
That is not something academics can do really, right?

593
00:57:10,304 --> 00:57:16,516
So from TRL 3 to TRL 6 or TRL 7, academics are completely on a lost ground.

594
00:57:16,784 --> 00:57:19,264
They will not even know what a certification is.

595
00:57:19,470 --> 00:57:28,464
And if I tell a PhD student, whatever you have done, do it 100 times, the student will run away because I cannot publish a paper by doing the same thing a thousand times, right?

596
00:57:28,544 --> 00:57:29,264
Why would I do that?

597
00:57:29,344 --> 00:57:29,504
Right?

598
00:57:29,774 --> 00:57:35,908
So therefore, academia is not well suited to take anything from TRL 3 to TRL 6 or TRL 7.

599
00:57:36,144 --> 00:57:43,504
And but but and then once you reach TRL 6, TRL 7, then you can start a company, you can start selling, you can start earning revenues.

600
00:57:43,664 --> 00:57:47,076
But who will do this TRL 3 to TRL 7, right?

601
00:57:47,278 --> 00:57:50,884
There is no agency in the country which is ready to take up that work.

602
00:57:51,104 --> 00:57:54,308
All CSIR labs they work on their own technologies.

603
00:57:54,606 --> 00:58:00,384
The CSIR labs have no mandate to connect with academic institutions around them, right?

604
00:58:00,558 --> 00:58:04,704
Whatever they are doing, they are doing well, but they do that only for their own technologies.

605
00:58:04,864 --> 00:58:06,704
And they cannot even start a company.

606
00:58:06,798 --> 00:58:09,424
A CSIR scientist cannot even start a company.

607
00:58:09,614 --> 00:58:17,664
They develop something up to a certain level, they wait for an industry to come forward, take their technology, which unfortunately doesn't happen in this country, right?

608
00:58:17,902 --> 00:58:19,904
So therefore, they are also stuck there, right?

609
00:58:20,206 --> 00:58:24,624
They develop up to TRL 7, but they are stuck there because they cannot start their own companies.

610
00:58:24,878 --> 00:58:34,784
And academia is stuck at TRL 3 because they don't even know how to move forward, and there is nobody working with them to develop those technologies to a level where they can start a company.

611
00:58:34,864 --> 00:58:41,184
In many academic institutions, we can start companies, but we don't know how to traverse that last spot, right?

612
00:58:41,264 --> 00:58:43,780
That valley of death, how to overcome that.

613
00:58:44,366 --> 00:58:45,872
That we are not well versed with it.

614
00:58:46,094 --> 00:58:48,192
Therefore, academia is stuck at TRL 3.

615
00:58:48,462 --> 00:58:53,632
CSIR labs are stuck at TRL 6 or 7 because they don't know how to move forward beyond that.

616
00:58:53,902 --> 00:58:54,992
And then who else now?

617
00:58:55,072 --> 00:58:55,952
Who else will do that?

618
00:58:56,112 --> 00:59:01,712
And industry, academia collaborations, India is really on a very bad kind of a platform.

619
00:59:01,872 --> 00:59:04,032
India Academia Industry Collaborations.

620
00:59:04,112 --> 00:59:05,472
Recently I saw a report.

621
00:59:05,710 --> 00:59:10,532
We are ranked 91st in the world when it comes to academia industry collaborations.

622
00:59:10,766 --> 00:59:13,152
We were ranked 82nd two years ago.

623
00:59:13,326 --> 00:59:20,272
Now we have actually gone down, show me one academia industry collaboration at scale,

624
00:59:20,272 --> 00:59:22,000
And the solution to this sir?

625
00:59:22,318 --> 00:59:24,272
the government taking the Trump role.

626
00:59:25,072 --> 00:59:28,912
Government taking the that that government has to be that enabler.

627
00:59:29,152 --> 00:59:35,552
Government has to tell the industries that, you know, whatever percentage of your revenues, not only CSR.

628
00:59:35,726 --> 00:59:39,392
CSR, there are so many players wanting that CSR money, right?

629
00:59:39,598 --> 00:59:44,512
You know, say that some percentage of your revenues, you need to collaborate with academia, right?

630
00:59:44,686 --> 00:59:51,792
You decide whether you want to collaborate on basic research or you want to collaborate at TRL 3 or TRL 4, whatever it is.

631
00:59:51,952 --> 00:59:56,260
But you have to invest certain amount of your revenues in working with academia.

632
00:59:56,512 --> 00:59:59,712
You do that, you know, India will be a totally different country.

633
00:59:59,872 --> 01:00:02,912
Our industries will benefit, our academia will benefit.

634
01:00:03,086 --> 01:00:07,152
Now there is a hand holding that is happening, the TRL 3 further, you know.

635
01:00:07,552 --> 01:00:10,992
I think this is, you know, the relationship needs to develop, right?

636
01:00:11,152 --> 01:00:11,716
You want to be able to do that.

637
01:00:12,112 --> 01:00:14,628
You cannot live in fractured environments.

638
01:00:15,632 --> 01:00:22,672
Government wants some kind of a love marriage to happen between academia and industry, which has not happened in 75 years, 80 years.

639
01:00:22,752 --> 01:00:24,420
Now there is no reason why it will happen.

640
01:00:24,686 --> 01:00:26,032
Government has to arrange a marriage.

641
01:00:26,592 --> 01:00:31,552
You have to mandate that you know, like all Indian marriages, they will find love eventually.

642
01:00:31,872 --> 01:00:37,152
Once you start working with a set of institutions, you will actually find that you know these are great people.

643
01:00:37,392 --> 01:00:38,592
I love working with them.

644
01:00:38,830 --> 01:00:41,924
And then once they start working with them, a relationship will build.

645
01:00:42,126 --> 01:00:48,512
And then a lot of these good things that are happening in academia will see the light of the day, and then industry will also become innovative.

646
01:00:48,718 --> 01:00:49,592
Oh, yeah,

647
01:00:49,592 --> 01:00:52,432
that way it will be a win-win for everyone.

648
01:00:52,512 --> 01:00:54,592
I think government has to be that enabler.

649
01:00:54,798 --> 01:00:56,672
Government needs to, you know, bell that cat.

650
01:00:56,752 --> 01:01:06,500
And unless we do that, I think all this, you know, saying, telling industry to work with academia and all of that, isn't really, you know, making a big difference on the ground.

651
01:01:07,502 --> 01:01:20,740
Before I let you go, Professor, because honestly, I would love to continue this conversation, but because of the positive of time, I would very humbly like to invite you back again because there's just so much more that I'd love to explore with you.

652
01:01:21,312 --> 01:01:23,952
it's been a very, very insightful discussion.

