Collaborations are good.

658
01:01:52,432 --> 01:01:54,992
I would like to see more and more international collaborations.

659
01:01:55,152 --> 01:02:02,272
In fact, you know, one of my op-eds in a newspaper, I even wrote that, you know, a thousand PhD students from India, right?

660
01:02:02,512 --> 01:02:07,872
We should allow them to spend a year abroad in top universities worldwide, right?

661
01:02:08,046 --> 01:02:11,152
You just enable them to go for a year, right?

662
01:02:11,406 --> 01:02:19,472
In MIT, Stanford, top universities in Europe, uh, you know, anywhere, right, where where which are doing great work, and let them come back after a year, right?

663
01:02:19,694 --> 01:02:23,312
Along with it, their faculty can spend two months, three months in that lab.

664
01:02:23,406 --> 01:02:26,832
Because there is so much to learn from these different cultures, right?

665
01:02:26,912 --> 01:02:38,432
After all, if you look at the Nobel Prizes, the quality of research, all of that that is happening, I think at the end of the day, there are certain ways they are doing things, which is definitely helping them, right?

666
01:02:38,734 --> 01:02:41,764
So, therefore, I think we must enable those international collaborations.

667
01:02:42,032 --> 01:02:47,076
We must not be living in a shell and thinking that we are the best in the world No, no, no.

668
01:02:47,232 --> 01:02:49,152
I was not coming from there, don't get me wrong, sir.

669
01:02:49,312 --> 01:02:52,992
I was also trying to kind of let me add to what I meant by collaborations.

670
01:02:53,102 --> 01:02:55,972
It was not just academic, it was also industrial.

671
01:02:56,272 --> 01:03:01,476
For example, us doing a lot of work with Japan when it comes down to the semiconductor space.

672
01:03:01,712 --> 01:03:16,100
So I was coming from that point of view that if we have such a rich ecosystem internally, should it not be something of a hybrid where we are also encouraging our own industry and collaborating with the Japan because they've been forerunners when it comes to semiconductors?

673
01:03:16,512 --> 01:03:17,860
That's what probably I was trying to get at.

674
01:03:18,574 --> 01:03:23,776
No, no, I think there like what we were discussing earlier, you know, learn from wherever it is available.

675
01:03:23,936 --> 01:03:26,468
Industry also needs to learn how to do things, right?

